"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1031311-chamber-similarity-lair-traits-and-primordial-pathways#post1031311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The examples given for imposing Lair Traits in locations similar to a Beast's Chambers (p.101-102) appear to relate more to opening Primordial Pathways, and the penalties listed here are very different from those listed in the Primordial Pathways section. Are the similarity penalties listed there actually relevant to opening Pathways, or are they only applied to Trait imposition?</div> </div> </div> </div>The wording in the section itself appears to suggest the penalties in question apply to both actions, with the line in the Primordial Pathways writeup about &quot;incurring an additional dice penalty based on how well the location matches&quot; seeming to indicate that the two tables are both considered for rolls to open a Pathway.<br /> <br /> There was a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways\">fairly lengthy discussion topic</a> about this a couple months ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel